# pyenv
#   For a library or package, you might want to ignore these files since the 
#   project is intended to be used by others, in which case you should
#   remove them from this file.
# .python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#598, it is recommended to include Pipfile.lock in version control.
#   However, in case of collaboration, if you are using a tool like pyenv,
#   you might want to ignore Pipfile.lock if you want to keep your local environment 
#   consistent with others.
# Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, it is generally recommended to include poetry.lock in version control.
# poetry.lock

